      "format": "python_code_unconstrained",
      "content": "class EnsureFanOn(py_trees.behaviour.Behaviour):\n    def __init__(self, name, state_url, action_url):\n        super().__init__(name)\n        self.state_url = state_url\n        self.action_url = action_url\n\n    def update(self):\n        # Check current state\n        resp = http_client.get(self.state_url)\n        if resp.status_code == 200 and resp.json() == \"on\":\n            return Status.SUCCESS  # Already on\n\n        # Turn it on\n        resp = http_client.post(self.action_url)\n        return Status.SUCCESS if resp.status_code == 200 else Status.FAILURE\n\n\nclass SetFanSpeed(py_trees.behaviour.Behaviour):\n    def __init__(self, name, speed_url, speed_value):\n        super().__init__(name)\n        self.speed_url = speed_url\n        self.speed_value = speed_value\n\n    def update(self):\n        # Set the fan speed\n        resp = http_client.post(self.speed_url, json={\"speed\": self.speed_value})\n        return Status.SUCCESS if resp.status_code == 200 else Status.FAILURE\n\n\n# Create the behavior tree\nensure_fan_on = EnsureFanOn(\n    name=\"Ensure Fan On\",\n    state_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/kitchen/artifacts/kitchenFan/properties/state\",\n    action_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/kitchen/artifacts/kitchenFan/turn_on\"\n)\n\nset_fan_speed = SetFanSpeed(\n    name=\"Set Fan Speed to High\",\n    speed_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/kitchen/artifacts/kitchenFan/set_speed\",\n    speed_value=\"high\"\n)\n\n# Sequence to ensure fan is on before setting speed\nsequence = py_trees.composites.Sequence(name=\"Set Fan Speed Sequence\", memory=True, children=[ensure_fan_on, set_fan_speed])\n\ntree = sequence",
      "explanation": "The behavior tree is designed to set the fan speed to 'high' in the kitchen. It consists of two custom behaviors:\n\n1. **EnsureFanOn**: This behavior checks if the kitchen fan is already on. If it is not, it sends a request to turn it on. It returns `Status.SUCCESS` if the fan is on or successfully turned on, and `Status.FAILURE` if it fails to turn on.\n\n2. **SetFanSpeed**: This behavior sets the fan speed to 'high'. It sends a request to set the speed and returns `Status.SUCCESS` if successful, otherwise `Status.FAILURE`.\n\nThese behaviors are combined in a `Sequence` composite node, which ensures that the fan is turned on before attempting to set the speed. The `memory=True` parameter ensures that if the fan is already on, the sequence will proceed directly to setting the speed without re-checking the fan state on subsequent ticks.",
